Neon spaces (M6): delete browsing data per space, and clear a space's data.

The "Delete browsing data" dialog (Ctrl+Shift+Delete, settings) gets a scope:
the space its settings tab is in, chosen by default, or all spaces, which also
covers the global context (the default partition). With one space chosen it
offers only the data a space keeps apart (cookies and site data, cached files)
and says that history, downloads, passwords and autofill are shared. The two
counters count the partitions in scope; the stock ones read the default
partition only. Deleting from all spaces waits until the per-container
removals are done.

"Clear this space's data..." in a space's menu in the switcher row and "Clear
data" on the Spaces settings page delete a space's cookies, site storage and
cache (all time) after a confirmation, keep the space and its tabs, and reload
its loaded tabs (containers_api::ClearContainerStorage, as deleting a space
does).

Adds containers_api::GetStoragePartitionConfig and ListUsedContainerIds,
chrome/browser/ui/neon/spaces/space_data.{h,cc}, space_data_handler.{h,cc},
chrome/browser/ui/views/neon/spaces/space_clear_confirmation.{h,cc} and the
dialog's settings-neon-space-scope element.
